<Base title="Cognitive Behavioral Therapy for Addiction" description="CBT in residential treatment and detox step-down at Experience Recovery in Santa Ana — individual and group cognitive behavioral therapy for substance use." path="/services/cognitive-behavioral-therapy/" keywords="CBT rehab Orange County, cognitive behavioral therapy addiction Santa Ana">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/services/">Services</a> / CBT</p>
    <h1>Cognitive behavioral therapy</h1>
    <p class="lede">CBT is one of the therapies we use because it has a research base for substance use and for the anxiety and depression that travel with it. It is not the only tool on campus.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap prose">
    <p>In residential treatment, CBT shows up in individual sessions and in groups: mapping triggers, testing the thoughts that make use feel inevitable, and practicing replacements that survive a Friday night in Orange County, not just a worksheet.</p>
    <p>If someone needs a different frame — trauma-focused work, motivational interviewing, skills for emotional dysregulation — we use those too. Insurance reviewers understand CBT language; that is a documentation fact, not a reason to pretend it is the whole of treatment.</p>
  </div></section>
